     I think the reasoning there is backwards.  If conflict
was tracked as a conduct, you could examine #conduct feedback
before and after trying on an unknown ring.  The change from
"you haven't caused conflict" to "you have caused conflict"
would allow players to recognize a ring of conflict without
risk of triggering any hostile monster activity.

     The user interface shouldn't be able to give away such
information.  The game would probably have to hide conflict-
less conduct until discovery of the ring (or #invoke of the
caveman's quest scepter, or game end).  I'm sure that anyone
trying to maintain conflict-less conduct would object to
having the fact that they'd already broken it be hidden from
them.


